<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre Nkurunziza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1964–2020</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre Nkurunziza was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> former rebel commander of the CNDD-FDD who became president of Burundi in 2005, after the civil war. His decision to seek a disputed third term in 2015 led to protests, a failed coup attempt and a wave of repression and emigration. He stepped down in 2020 and died shortly afterwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-nkurunziza.jpg" alt="Pierre Nkurunziza" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Copyright World Economic Forum/Eric Miller, (mailto:emiller@iafrica.com) · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pierre_Nkurunziza_-_World_Economic_Forum_on_Africa_2008.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
